  "id": "a9f76c84-e9b6-58f7-8edb-989c186f4c9e",
  "slug": "upside-down-banana-bread-recipe-12062332",
  "name": "Upside Down Banana Bread",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "This upside-down banana bread pops out of the pan with a caramelized banana top. It makes a rich, delicious side dish or even a light dessert. Also a great use for overripe bananas.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C). Coat a 9x5-inch loaf pan with cooking spray; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Combine flour, baking soda, and salt in a bowl; set aside. Combine 3/4 cup brown sugar and 1/2 cup butter in a large bowl; beat with an electric mixer on medium-high speed until lighter in color, scraping down sides of bowl as needed, about 2 minutes. Reduce speed to medium-low and add eggs, 1 at a time, beating well after each addition. Add vanilla and beat until incorporated. Using a spatula, fold in mashed bananas until just combined. Fold in half of the flour mixture until just combined. Repeat with remaining flour mixture. Set batter aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Melt remaining 1/4 cup butter in a small saucepan over medium heat. Once bubbling, add remaining 1/2 cup brown sugar and let simmer, stirring occasionally, until sugar has dissolved and mixture bubbles and thickens, about 2 minutes. Pour sugar mixture into prepared pan. Arrange banana pieces on top of sugar mixture side by side, cut side down. Pour batter over bananas and spread evenly."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a wooden pick inserted in center comes out clean, about 1 hour. Let cool in the pan on a wire rack for 5 minutes. Invert cake onto plate and cool at least 20 minutes before serving. Recipe Developed by Anna Porter"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 65,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
  "difficulty": "hard",
